   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{CB3A0B1E5FD7CB22}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "I. Situation:"
     m_sContent "<h2>I. Situation:</h2>"\
     "<b>Time & Weather:</b>"\
     "<i>Time - 06:02"\
     "Weather - Cloudy, Some Low Fog</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Situation:</b>"\
     "<i>A Canadian Mechanized Company (-) with a attached USMC AH-1S flight is tasked with securing a beachhead on Kulgoyev at the Mineraly Military Site & Harbour, while the Soviets have been anticipating a landing for some time, sending units to fortify themselves and have air suppport on the way to the island.</i>"
    }
    GC_Briefing "{534FD20A6F0467ED}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "A. Enemy Forces:"
     m_sContent "<h2>A. Enemy Forces:</h2>"\
     "<b>Equipment:</b>"\
     "<i>USSR are equipped with their standard WARSAW Pact weaponry, AK series, RPG7s, PKMs."\
     "Wearing the standard USSR uniform of Tan with greenish helmet..</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Known Strength:</b>"\
     "<i>1x Rifle Batallion (-)</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Location:</b>"\
     "<i>- Last known locations of enemy forces;"\
     "1x Rifle Platoon (+) is located near the Red Beach"\
     "1x Rifle Platoon is located on the Yellow Beach"\
     "1x Rifle Section (+) is located on the White Beach"\
     "1x Rifle Company (-) is located on the Factory"\
     "1x Rifle Platoon (-) is located on the East of the Factory"\
     "1x Rifle Platoon (-) is located on the West of the Apartments"\
     "1x Mechanized Company is located between Apartments and Military Site</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Capabilities:</b>"\
     "<i>Access to RPGs, PKMs, VOGs, Flares."\
     "Vehicles include BMP-1Ps, BRDMs, ZSU-23-2, potential MI-24."\
     "QRF in the vicinity to react to our landing.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>MLCOA:</b>"\
     "<i>Lure us in after we land on a beach before conducting a counter attack to push us out of the landing site.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>MDCOA:</b>"\
     "<i>Lure us in after we land on a beach before ambushing us as we move towards our objectives, sending BMPs to engage our LAVs and if we take enough time call in a MI-24 for support.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Defensive Fires:</b>"\
     "<i>No known in-direct threat at this time.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Airthreat:</b>"\
     "<i>Mi-24 squadron in the area.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Morale:</b>"\
     "<i>Very High.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>CBRN Threat:</b>"\
     "<i>The enemy pose no CBRN Threat as of now.</i>"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{051D80A5FD52B71B}" {
     m_iOrder 2
     m_sTitle "Main Briefing (MUST READ ALL)"
     m_sContent "<h2>Shit Simple Brief:</h2>"\
     "<i>Congrats you're getting the shit simple briefing but also the most required/restricted one."\
     ""\
     "Here are the Mission Maker's Intents for you guys.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Mission Maker Intent:</b>"\
     "<i>- You start out with 2x tickets and a ZSU-23-2 Ural Truck, located South-East of the military site at 065 078."\
     "- Once you enter a vehicle you WILL NOT be able to exit it, there'll be a 60sec timer. "\
     "- No you're not allowed to skimp the ZSU-23-2 Ural Truck and go on Foot. Against the Mission Maker Intent.. Don't worry you'll be rewarded soon."\
     "- TP to the ZSU will close after 10min ingame"\
     ""\
     "- Main goal/victory for you is to target & destroy the AH-1S' and a smaller priority the UH-1H</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>DO NOT AIM, FIRE NOR FOCUS THE ZSU ON THE MAIN PLAYER FORCE NOR LAVS IN THE WATER, AT LEAST NOT UNTIL THEYV'VE SECURED A BEACH LANDING (5-10MIN AFTER THEY LAND)</b>"\
     ""\
     "- Once BLUFOR captures either the Factory or the Fuel Depot, the Mi-24 will be unlocked located at 021 008."\
     "- Either kill yourself or ram the ZSU-23-2 Truck towards the players and respawn"\
     ""\
     "<i>Teleport to the Mi-24 and the restrictions are now off, you have limited armaments:"\
     "16x S-5 Rockets"\
     "3x R-60 AA Missiles"\
     "-- NOTE, you cannot lock them on because WCS hates you, fire normally and they will have a *chance* to self lock onto a helicopter but its not as good as proper lock.. yeah I know, I really tried."\
     "1400x Ball Turret YAK-B"\
     ""\
     "<b>DO NOT AIM, FIRE NOR FLY ANYWHERE CLOSE TO THE BLUFOR'S SPAWN ISLAND NORTH, If this is at any point failed I will make a Kill Zone destroying both you and the helicopter by even sniffing the island in the next patch while you're in breach of the Mission Maker Intent and my trust towards the playerbase</b>"\
     ""\
     "- BLUFOR will have at least 6x FIM92 Stingers, you're best recommended advice AND the intended fly pattern of a Mi-24 is;</i>"\
     ""\
     "<h2>- Fly low (NOE Tree Top Level)"\
     "- Fly Fast (Max Speed)"\
     "- Strike Hard</h2>"\
     ""\
     "<h2>- Good Luck & Have Fun</h2>"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{BB145974F17EA4FB}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "B. Friendly Forces:"
     m_sContent "<h2>B. Friendly Forces</h2>"\
     "<b>a. Disposition:</b>"\
     "<i>All Canadian & attached USMC forces (YOU) are located at the island north fo Mineraly, markd on map.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>b. Higher Units Mission:</b>"\
     "<i>Company has been tasked with securing a beach head on Kulgoyev</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>c. Composition:</b>"\
     "<i>1x Mechanized Canadian Company (-)"\
     "1x Flight of AH-1S's"\
     "1x UH-1H - FAC(A)"\
     ""\
     "Ground FAC is main Air Controller</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>d. Strength:</b>"\
     "<i>29 COY - At 80x Man Strength."\
     "Stingray Flight - At 4x Man Strength"\
     "Goldfish - At 3x Man Strength</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>e. Supporting Fires:</b>"\
     "<i>Naval guns will provide a smoke firemission upon the decided landing site.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>f. Attachments/Detachments:</b>"\
     "<i>2x AH-1S's"\
     "1x UH-1H - FAC(A)</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>g. Additional Ammunition</b>"\
     "<i>Provided in the LAVIIs.</i>"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{E64EA95853DB7336}" {
     m_iOrder 4
     m_sTitle "II. Mission (Must Read):"
     m_sContent "<h2>II: Mission</h2>"\
     "<i>Secure Mineraly and the infastructure around it to establish ourselves on the island of Kulguyev"\
     ""\
     "Choose between the Fuel Depot or the Factory to serve as a established foothold for reinforcements before proceeding towards the Apartments & Military Site."\
     ""\
     "- Naval Gun Support will conduct a smoke firemission on ONE of the beaches we land on (Area Trigger)"\
     "- LAVs has Smoke Launchers as well.</i>"\
     ""\
     ""\
     "<b>Not for AH-1S & UH-1H from Mission Maker:</b>"\
     "<i>- If you're shot down there'll be UH-1H spawning (1x per Helo), should you run out of helicopters, there's a crate near your teleporter so you can JOIN THE REAL FIGHT, GROUND POUNDER."\
     ""\
     "- DO NOT fly beyond 500m from the AO in an attempt to hunt the spawn location of the Mi-24, against Mission Maker Intent and breaks my trust towards the community</i>"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{3D16D7843593F10B}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "III. Execution:"
     m_sContent "<h2>III: Execution</h2>"\
     "<b>Intent:</b>"\
     "<i>"\
     "Amphibious land at Mineraly to secure vital infastructure and eliminating the soviet presence in the area. "\
     ""\
     "<b>1. Concept of the Operation:</b>"\
     "<i>Company Commander's Discretion."\
     "It is adviced to utilize the AH-1S and UH-1H to recon the beaches for any ZU-23-2 that may be used as a naval defence weapon and help securing the airspace for the landing</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Maneuver</b>"\
     "<i>Company Commander's Discretion."\
     "It is adviced to secure either the Fuel Depot or the Factory to establish a local HQ for reinforcements before proceeding, while also making sure both Platoons are able to mutually support one another and not split off leading to the chance of them being cut off and decisively destroyed."\
     "</i>"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{48EA5707EE91C7BD}" {
     m_iOrder 6
     m_sTitle "IV. Sustainment:"
     m_sContent "<h2>IV: Sustainment</h2>"\
     "<b>a. SOP Variations</b>"\
     "<i>Dress: Standard Canadian Uniform"\
     "Equipment: Standard Canadian Loadout"\
     "Vehicle Loading:"\
     "- Whiskey Detachment rides with the PLT HQ LAV"\
     "- LAVIIs can carry 9x People incl crew.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>b. Logistical Support:</b>"\
     "<i>Replen Plan: None for 24h."\
     "Ammunition: Each man carries his own ammunition & LAVIIs carry additional ammunition."\
     "IPE: Helmets and body armour are to be worn at all times."\
     "Air has Rearm, 3000x Supplies to utilize to rearm their weapons at their spawned locations</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>c. Medical:</b>"\
     "<i>Location: Company Aid Post is to be setup by company medics."\
     "CASEVAC: By foot or with company asset like the UH-1H."\
     "Plan: Set up a casualty collection point and extract casualties to this point."\
     "Stretchers: None"\
     "Med Packs: Company medpack carried by company medic."\
     "Morphine: Every soldier carries 1+ stick of morphine.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>d. Vehicles:</b>"\
     "<i>9x LAVIIs"\
     "- LAVs has Smoke Launchers"\
     "Each LAV-IIs contains;"\
     "- 20x Bandages"\
     "- 20x Tourniquets"\
     "- 10x Morphine"\
     "- 48x Stanag Mags"\
     "- 12x M249 Boxes"\
     "- 12x Grenades"\
     "- 12x Smoke Grenades"\
     "- 8x 40mm Grenade"\
     "- 24x 40mm Flares"\
     "- 2x LAWs"\
     "- 1x ANPRC77"\
     ""\
     "Each LAVII HQ carries an additional"\
     "2x FIM92 Stingers (6x Total)"\
     ""\
     "1x AH-1S"\
     "- 19x 70mm HE M229"\
     "- 2x Aim-9 Sidewinder"\
     "- 450x 20x102mm M197 Gun"\
     ""\
     "1x AH-1S"\
     "- 19x 70mm HE M229"\
     "- 8x M299 Hellfire Missiles"\
     "- 450x 20x102mm M197 Gun"\
     ""\
     "1x UH-1H"\
     "- 14x HEDP Rockets"\
     "- 2x M240 Machineguns"\
     ""\
     "3x UH-1Hs will be provided for the helicopters if they were to be shot down (1x per Heli)"\
     "</i>"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{D95F63FC2666C096}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "V. Command & Signals:"
     m_sContent "<h2>V. Command & Signal:</h2>"\
     "<b>I. Chain of Command:</b>"\
     "<i>29, 29A, 21, 22, etc</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>II. Callsigns:</b>"\
     "<i>Company HQ --------------------------- 2"\
     "- Company OC ------------------------- 29"\
     "- Company 2iC ------------------------ 29A - Alpha"\
     "- Company CSM ---------------------- 29D - Delta"\
     "- FAC -------------------------------------- 29K - Kilo"\
     "- FAC(A) --------------------------------- 29S - SIERRA"\
     ""\
     "Platoon HQ ---------------------------- 21"\
     "- Platoon Leader -------------------- 21 Sunray"\
     "- Platoon Warrant ------------------ 21 Sunray Minor "\
     "1st Section --------------------------- 21 Alpha"\
     "2nd Section -------------------------- 21 Bravo"\
     "3rd Section --------------------------- 21 Charlie"\
     "Weapons Detachment ---------- 21 Whisky"\
     ""\
     "Platoon HQ ---------------------------- 22"\
     "- Platoon Leader -------------------- 22 Sunray"\
     "- Platoon Warrant ------------------ 22 Sunray Minor "\
     "1st Section --------------------------- 22 Alpha"\
     "2nd Section -------------------------- 22 Bravo"\
     "3rd Section --------------------------- 22 Charlie"\
     "Weapons Detachment ---------- 22 Whisky"\
     ""\
     "1st AH-1S ----------------------------- Stingray 1-1"\
     "2nd AH-1S ---------------------------- Stingray 1-2"\
     "UH-1H ---------------------------------- Goldfish 1-1 </i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>- - - Vehicle/LAV Callsigns when Inf dismounted:</b>"\
     "<i>Z29 or Zulu 29"\
     "Zulu 21 Alpha"\
     "Zulu 21 Bravo"\
     "Etc.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>III. Frequencies:</b>"\
     "<i>Company Net ------------ 48.00Mhz"\
     "1st Platoon Net -------- 47.00Mhz"\
     "2nd Platoon Net ------- 49.00Mhz"\
     "Air Net --------------------- 50.00Mhz</i>"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{0CECD103D5235E30}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "VI. Mission Notes:"
     m_sContent "<h2>Mission Notes:</h2>"\
     "<b>Timelimit:</b>"\
     "<i>60m (Can be increased by GM's Discretion)</i>"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Victory/Defeat Conditions:</h2>"\
     "<b>- Canadian Victory; </b>"\
     "- Fuel Depot OR Factory Secured"\
     "- Apartment Secured"\
     "- Military Site Secured"\
     ""\
     "<b>- Canadian Defeat</b>"\
     " - Suffering 90% casualties or Timelimit is reached</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>BLUFOR Respawns:</b>"\
     "<i>BLUFOR will get a Respawn Wave Window (Spawn everyone in spectator) and 90x Tickets once they secure either Fuel Depot OR Factory</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>GM Discretion as usual.</b>"
    }
    GC_Briefing "{662D27BD8246A4BA}" {
     m_iOrder 9
     m_sTitle "VII. Air Control Manual (FAC MUST READ)"
     m_sContent "<h2>Table of Contents:</h2>"\
     "<b>- Different Types</b>"\
     "<b>- Legends / Brevity Codes</b>"\
     "<b>- Example Transmissions between JTAC & Aircraft pilots:</b>"\
     "<b>- Formats for Transmissions</b> "\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>1) Type 1 Control.</h2>"\
     "<i><b>Type 1 control</b> is used when the JTAC/FAC must visually acquire the attacking Aircraft and the Mark / Target for control of each individual attack prior to weapons release / launch. </i> "\
     "<h2>(2) Type 2 Control.</h2>"\
     "<i><b>Type 2 control</b> is used when the JTAC/FAC must visually acquire the attacking Aircraft OR the Mark / Target for control of each individual attack prior to weapons release / launch.</i> "\
     "<h2>(3) Type 3 Control.</h2>"\
     "<i><b>Type 3 control</b> is used when the JTAC/FAC requires the ability to provide clearance for multiple attacks within a single engagement subject to specific attack restrictions. Type 3 control does not require the JTAC to visually acquire the aircraft or the target</i> "\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Legends / Brevity Codes</h2>"\
     "<b>- VISUAL</b> <i>= Sighting of a friendly aircraft/ground position. Opposite of BLIND.</i>"\
     "<b>- BLIND</b> <i>= No visual contact of friendly aircraft/ground position. Opposite of VISUAL. </i>"\
     "<b>- NO JOY</b> <i>= Aircrew does not have visual contact with the target / bandit / landmark. Opposite of TALLY. </i>"\
     "<b>- TALLY</b> <i>= Sighting of a target, non-friendly aircraft, landmark, or enemy position. Opposite of NO JOY. </i>"\
     "<b>- BOT</b> <i>= Bomb On Target</i>"\
     "<b>- TOT</b> <i>= Time On Target</i>"\
     "<b>- TTT</b> <i>= Time To Target</i>"\
     "<b>- SEAD</b> <i>= Suppression of Enemy Air Defenses</i>"\
     "<b>- ABORT</b><i>= Directive call to cease action/attack/event/mission. Do not release ordnance.</i>"\
     "<b>- CLEARED HOT</b><i>=  Ordnance release is authorized in Type 1 or 2 terminal attack controls. </i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>- CLEARED TO ENGAGE</b><i>=  JTAC Type 3 control clearance. Attack aircraft flight leaders may initiate attacks within the parameters imposed by the JTAC. Attack platforms will provide a “Commencing Engagement” call prior to engaging targets and an “Engagement Complete” call to JTAC, indicating completion of ordnance release.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>- CONTINUE</b><i>=  Continue present maneuver. Does not imply a change in clearance to engage or expend ordnance.</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>- CONTINUE DRY</b><i>=  Continue present maneuver, ordnance release not authorized. Used to provide approval to aircraft to continue the pass without expending ordnance during Type 1, 2, or 3* controls. (*JTAC must use “Type 3, Continue Dry” for dry Type 3 controls.) </i> "\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Example 5-Line Brief Transmission:</h2>"\
     "<b>Deuce31 (JTAC):</b>"\
     "<i>“Deuce 31, Broadsword 11, 5-line, Type 2 control, BOT, rockets and guns, my position is checkpoint 295 marked by IR strobe, northwest 200, single technical vehicle marked by IR SPARKLE, make all attacks over my right shoulder, left pull, keep all effects of fires west of MSR Clovis.”</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Broadsword 11 (A/C):</b>"\
     "<i>“Deuce 31 copies over your right shoulder, left pull, keep all effects of fires west of MSR Clovis, pushing.”</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Deuce31 (JTAC):</b>"\
     "<i>“Deuce 31, CONTINUE.”</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Broadsword 11 (A/C):</b>"\
     "<i>“Deuce 31 and flight, VISUAL, TALLY, IN.”</i>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Deuce31 (JTAC):</b>"\
     "<i>“Deuce 31 and flight, CLEARED HOT.”</i> "\
     ""\
     "<h2>Example Situation Update Transmission:</h2>"\
     "<b>Deuce31 (JTAC):</b>"\
     "<i>“Deuce 31, Broadsword 11, Friendlies are two companies in the vicinity of OP 2, one on the high ground and the other in a blocking position to the east. I am with the company on the high ground. There is also a Recon team at the northwest tip of Black Mountain, arty is firecapped at Firebase 5E, firing generally west, Break.”</i>"\
     ""\
     "<i>“Current surface-to-air threat is a SA-6 at KJ 123 456, just west of MSR Tampa; target is light armored company attempting to flank us to the north and two companies dug in three klicks to our west, Over.”</i> "\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Format: Rotary-Wing Close Air Support 5-Line Brief</h2>"\
     "Do not transmit line numbers. Units of measure are standard unless briefed. Restrictions are mandatory readback (*). JTAC may request additional readback. "\
     ""\
     "- 1. Observer/Warning Order"\
     "“(Aircraft Call Sign) _____________ , "\
     "This Is (JTAC Call Sign) _____________ , Over\" "\
     "5-line, Type (1, 2, or 3) C, MOA (BOC or BOT), (Ordnance Requested)"\
     ""\
     "- 2. Friendly Location/Mark "\
     "\"My position_____________ (TRP, Grid, etc.) , "\
     "Marked by _____________ (VS-17, Beacon, IR Strobe, etc.)\""\
     ""\
     "- 3. Target location "\
     "\"Target location, _________________________\" "\
     "(Bearing [magnetic] and Range [meters], TRP, Grid, etc.) "\
     ""\
     "- 4. Target Description/Mark"\
     "\" _____________ (Target Description) ,"\
     "marked by _____________ (IR sparkle, Tracer, etc.)\""\
     ""\
     "- 5. Remarks/Restrictions "\
     "*Final Attack Headings (FAHs) LTL/PTL "\
     "Surface-to-air threat"\
     "*Danger Close and initials"\
     "Additional calls requested"\
     "Additional remarks (GTL, weather, hazards, friendly mark)"\
     "*TOT/TTT "\
     ""\
     "The RW CAS 5-line should be passed as one transmission. If the restrictions portion is lengthy, it may be a separate transmission. "\
     ""\
     "<h2>Format: Situation Update (Controller to Close Air Support Aircraft)</h2>"\
     "<b>Situation Update # ____________________________ (if applicable) </b>"\
     "- Friendly Situation (disposition / posture, locations)"\
     "- Threat Activity (surface-to-air threats observed: who, what, when, where)"\
     "- Target – General Enemy Situation (“SALUTE” format – size, activity, location, uniform, time, equipment)"\
     "- Clearance Authority (Who has final control?)"\
     "- Ordnance Requested"\
     "- Restrictions"\
     "- Hazards (weather, terrain, obstructions)"\
     "- Remarks (JTAC capabilities, to include TLE if appropriate)"\
     ""\
     "Note: - This briefing should be broad in scope and will not be used as a substitute for a 5-line OR a 9-Line CAS briefing. "
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{B553556E8F02F63A}" {
     m_iOrder 10
     m_sTitle "Game Mastering"
     m_sContent "<h2>Game Mastering</h2>"\
     "<b>- GameMasters, make sure the OPFOR Players enter their vehicle on mission start, they are not allowed to be on foot (They'll be rewarded)</b>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Outside of that;</b>"\
     "<i>This mission is not designed for game mastering and should only be manipulated for technical, administrative or diagnostic purposes.</i>"
    }
   }
  }
 }
}
